{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law limits, interest and return rules","requirement":"A landlord may hold a security deposit of no more than 1.5 months' rent, with yearly increases capped at 10%; the deposit is held in trust, earns interest for the tenant, and must be returned with an itemized list of deductions within 30 days.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; yearly increase max 10% of deposit","coverage_conditions":"Any landlord who collects a security deposit from a residential tenant; at lease inception the landlord may collect no more than 2.5 months' rent, counting the deposit and first month's rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Deposit-account rules differ by landlord's unit count (10 or more units may use a money market fund)"},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental, a term of not more than 125 consecutive days for a person whose permanent residence is elsewhere, is exempt from the deposit account and interest provisions.","penalty":"If the deposit is not returned within 30 days, the tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 et seq.","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act deposit return after domestic-violence lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days, notify the tenant within 3 business days where to collect it, and keep it available for 30 days.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a residential lease before expiration because of domestic violence under the Safe Housing Act; public housing authority tenants give notice under the relevant regulations.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
